<v Agent 2>OK, it made its way to an online news source that you subscribe to. Getting really specific. Would you agree? Looks awfully bad.
<v Agent 2>好的，它流传到你订阅的一个在线新闻源了。变得非常具体了。你同意吗？看起来糟透了。

00:57:34.860 --> 00:57:39.860
<v Reality Winner>It looks really bad.
<v Reality Winner>看起来确实很糟糕。

00:57:39.860 --> 00:57:47.600
<v Agent 2>So how'd you get it out of the office?
<v Agent 2>那你怎么把它带出办公室的？

00:57:47.600 --> 00:57:51.460
<v Reality Winner>Folded in half in my pantyhose.
<v Reality Winner>对折塞进连裤袜里。

00:57:51.460 --> 00:57:55.720
<v Agent 2>OK. And what did you do with it?
<v Agent 2>好的。你拿它做了什么？

00:57:55.720 --> 00:58:16.270
<v Reality Winner>Put it in an envelope and sent it to [RUMBLING]. That day, that week, it was just too much to sit back, and watch, and think, why do I have this job if I'm just going to sit back and be helpless? And it did-- it just-- sorry. I just thought that that was the final straw.
<v Reality Winner>放进信封，发给了[隆隆声]。那一天，那一周，仅仅是坐视不理，看着，心想，如果我只是坐视不理并表现得无能为力，我为什么还要这份工作？这简直——抱歉。我只是觉得那是最后一根稻草。

00:58:16.270 --> 00:58:29.550
<v Agent 2>It was just something that just kind of did it? Because you don't seem like the type to do this. I believe it. I want to believe it.
<v Agent 2>那只是某种事情发生的导火索吗？因为你看起来不像那种会做这种事的人。我相信它。我想相信它。

00:58:29.550 --> 00:59:01.990
<v Reality Winner>I'm not. I'm not. I want to go out with our special forces. I mean, that's why I got out of the Air Force. That's why I'm here in Augusta. I wanted my clearance back so I could apply for a deployment, and it was just at a time when I wasn't applying for any deployments. And I had seven or eight months left of a job that didn't mean anything to me, because it's Iran, and I'm a Pashto linguist. What am I doing translating Farsi?
<v Reality Winner>我不像。我不像。我想和我们的特种部队一起出去。我的意思是，这就是我离开空军的原因。这就是我在这儿奥古斯塔的原因。我想要回我的许可，这样我就能申请部署了，当时我没申请任何部署。我还有七八个月的工作，对我来说没什么意义，因为那是伊朗，而我是普什图语语言学家。我翻译波斯语算什么？

00:59:01.990 --> 00:59:30.900
<v Reality Winner>And it just-- I just felt really hopeless, and seeing that information that had been contested back and forth, and back and forth in the public domain for so long, trying to figure out with everything else that keeps getting leaked and keeps getting released, why isn't this getting out? Why isn't this getting out there? Why can't this be public?
<v Reality Winner>我只是感到非常绝望，看到那些在公共领域来回争论、争论了那么久的信息，看着所有其他不断被泄露和发布的信息，想弄明白为什么这个没有发布？为什么这没有流传出去？为什么不能公开？

00:59:30.900 --> 01:00:07.210
<v Ira Glass>Actors Emily Davis, TL Thompson, and Pete Simpson. As you may know, this was all in the news. The document that Reality Winner leaked to the website The Intercept was an intelligence report confirming Russian hacking in the 2016 election. She's still serving her five year sentence. Sounds design and music for the stage production by Sanae Yamada, and Jimin Breslford. Tina Satter's theatrical adaptation of the FBI transcript is called Is This a Room. They have a tour scheduled. Information at halfstraddle.com.
<v Ira Glass>演员艾米丽·戴维斯、TL·汤普森和皮特·辛普森。如你所知，这一切都在新闻里。雷亚蒂·温纳泄露给“拦截”（The Intercept）网站的文件是一份确认俄罗斯黑客干预2016年选举的情报报告。她还在服五年刑期。舞台制作的声音设计和音乐由萨娜·山田和吉敏·布雷斯福德提供。蒂娜·萨特对FBI记录的戏剧改编名为《这就是个房间》。他们有巡演计划。信息请查阅halfstraddle.com。

